(Death Quaker) wrote:

>I've been playing Nethack for years though have never quite gotten the
>mix of skill, patience, and luck needed to Ascend (legitimately).

	ditto.

>So--finally, and thanks if you're still reading this--here's the
>question: what's a Wizard to do when she can't find non-metal armor? I
>was high enough level I was attracting monsters who hit well and hard;
>I really needed a decent AC.

	Well, if you're trying to ascend, you have to make some smart
moves early. If playing for amusement (like me), it matters less.

	My favorite strategy is to set luck=1 by setting date to full
moon, then try to quaff from fountains on the early levels. You have a
1 in 30 chance of summoning a demon, who has a 19% chance of being
friendly and granting a wish.

	"a +4 silver dragon scale mail"  is my wish (+4 since I may
not know *any* scrolls yet, and don't want to screw it up w/over
enchantment.)

	This and a standard magic cloak makes for a great starting
character. May I also suggest enchanted wormteeth as a dandy weapon
for your wizard ? Great 'to hit' bonus, and a pretty good damage roll.


>Is it worth it, in that circumstance--especially since I only had a
>couple basic spells (force bolt, light, and magic missile)--to wear
>metal armor despite the restrictions on spell casting?

	Studded leather armor can be enchanted enough to get you
through much of the opening game, especially if you have other armor
you can enchant/damageproof as well. 

>Is it worth "wasting" scrolls of Enchant armor on your starting cloak
>of magic resistance in case you can't find anything better along the
>way?

	Yes, since the Magic Markers will let you write more of these
later.

>Should I have just played around longer in higher dungeon levels until
>I chanced to find some usable armor?

	The gnomish mines have a lot of good booty.



